-> Reference: `∪` (union) and `∩` (intersection) — on Set values, on
-> unresolved-but-finite scalar domains (materialized into a Set), and
-> on Schema values (∩ merges field constraints).
a = {1, 2, 3}
b = {2, 3, 4}
assert (a ∪ b) = {1, 2, 3, 4}
assert (a ∩ b) = {2, 3}

p ∈ Z
p > 0
p < 3
q ∈ Z
q > 2
q < 5
assert (p ∪ q) = {1, 2, 3, 4}

k = { x ∈ Number }
j = { y ∈ String }
merged = k ∩ j
assert { x = 1, y = "z" } ∈ merged
